# Commits that only renamed things, for `git blame` to skip.
#
# Turn it on once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Without it, blaming almost any file in `src/` credits the translation pass for
# nearly every line, and the history stops answering "why is this line here?" —
# which is the whole point of the way this repository comments.
#
# Only PURE renames belong here. Several commits from the same pass also fixed
# real defects the translation exposed, or moved a string into the catalogue;
# those are deliberately absent, because skipping them would hide the change.
# Their subjects say so — anything with ", e ..." did a second thing.

